  "responsibility": "One writer at a time per board: a lease file beside the board, an agent's claim on it, and who holds it",
  "description": "ADR 0016. The lease lives in the vault, so every server on the vault sees the same exclusion; a dead holder costs one lease rather than wedging the board. A person's take-back (takeBackBoard) holds the lease with the claim revoked and gives it straight back, and answers the claim that stood. The claims, the lock watch and the lines agents said they were doing are process memory, and forgetBoardMemory drops all of it when a server stops, leaving the leases in each vault as they are.",
